        "title": {
          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Ravi drew a graph of a cycle ride, plotting distance against time.\n\"The steeper the line, the faster the cycle,\" said his teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "graph",
          "uniform motion",
          "at rest"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A distance-time graph shows how distance changes with time. A straight slanting line means constant speed. A flat line means the object is at rest.\nA steeper line means a higher speed. For uniform motion the graph is a straight line.\nSpeed equals distance divided by time. If the graph shows 60 km in 2 hours, the speed is 30 km per hour."
        }
      },
